                    [3 "Disadvantage on attack rolls and saving throws"]
                    [4 "Hit point maximum halved"]
                    [5 "Speed reduced to 0"]
                    [6 "Death"]]}]
          [:p "If an already exhausted creature suffers another effect that causes exhaustion, its current level of exhaustion increases by the amount specified in the effect’s description."]
          [:p "A creature suffers the effect of its current level of exhaustion as well as all lower levels. For example, a creature suffering level 2 exhaustion has its speed halved and has disadvantage on ability checks."]
          [:p "An effect that removes exhaustion reduces its level as specified in the effect’s description, with all exhaustion effects ending if a creature’s exhaustion level is reduced below 1."]
          [:p "Finishing a long rest reduces a creature’s exhaustion level by 1, provided that the creature has also ingested some food and drink."]]}
